Z||000011||DrRodey||02-19-2001||12:50 PM||||Bad thing about translators... They translate word for word, not only does it rarely make sence, it usually means something completely different based on context.  There are many words in any language, especially German that have multiple meanings based on how they are used in a sentence.  A translator will give you a general idea but won't be an exact meaning.<P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">          <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
